Description: gdk: GdkMemoryFormat, GdkColorState and GdkCicpParams under GTK 4's names
 The depth and the colour state of a GtkGLArea's picture. GdkMemoryFormat has
 the five formats an area renders in, with GTK 4's names and values;
 GdkColorState and GdkCicpParams carry ITU-T H.273 code points (colour
 primaries, transfer characteristics, matrix coefficients, range), with GTK 4's
 four getters (sRGB, linear sRGB, Rec. 2100 PQ and linear) and the builder for
 any other. A colour state is a description, not a conversion.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-26
